Next, the Settings tab buttons. Add a new section before About:

```xaml
            <Button Content="About" Click="AboutButton_Click" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Margin="0,24,0,0" Padding="16,6"/>
```

Insert before About:

```xaml
            <TextBlock Text="Cached Workshop Data" Foreground="{DynamicResource AccentBlue}"
                       FontWeight="Bold" Margin="0,24,0,6"/>
            <TextBlock Text="Deletes the SteamCMD workshop content cache (already-downloaded workshop items). SteamCMD itself and your installed mods are not affected. This downloads again the next time a mod is downloaded or updated."
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource FgText}" Opacity="0.7" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
            <Button Content="Delete Cached Workshop Mods" Click="ClearWorkshopCache_Click" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Padding="16,6" Margin="0,0,0,0"
                    Background="#5C1A1A" Foreground="{DynamicResource FgText}"/>
```

Hmm, about the red background: `#5C1A1A` — but note that the app's style sets the Foreground of all buttons to FgText. For the accent green button, they explicitly set Foreground="White". As a "destructive" style, I'll decide to set Background="#4A2030" Foreground="White". Keep it simple.

Next, the code-behind:
1. Add the `ClearTileModeHelpers` private method + wire it into the three view handlers.
2. Add the ClearWorkshopCache_Click handler.

Edit of the view handler — example from InstalledView_Checked:

```csharp
