```
After the InstalledTiles line, add:
```csharp
        InstalledTileSizeLabel.Visibility = tiles ? Visibility.Visible : Visibility.Collapsed;
        InstalledTileSizer.Visibility = tiles ? Visibility.Visible : Visibility.Collapsed;
```

Same for the Downloads and Uninstalled ones.

And the cache handler, put it near the Settings section or in the Updater tab section. I'll add it after PickModsFolder or in the Settings area. Placement:

```csharp
    private void ClearWorkshopCache_Click(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)
    {
        var confirm = MessageBox.Show(
            "Delete the cached Workshop mod files under SteamCMD's content folder?\n\n" +
            "Only downloaded workshop item caches are deleted — SteamCMD itself and your " +
            "installed mods folder are not affected. Any cached mods that PZ needs again " +
            "will be downloaded on the next download or update.",
            "Confirm Cache Clear", MessageBoxButton.YesNo, MessageBoxImage.Warning);
        if (confirm != MessageBoxResult.Yes) return;

        try
        {
            SteamCmdService.ClearWorkshopContentCache();
            AppendLog("Cleared cached Workshop content.");
            StatusText.Text = "Cleared cached Workshop content.";
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            MessageBox.Show($"Could not clear the Workshop content cache: {ex.Message}");
            AppendLog($"FAILED to clear Workshop content cache: {ex.Message}", "ERROR");
        }
    }
```

`using System.IO;` is already present. `System.MessageBox` — the using for System.Windows is present. OK.

